      "math_academy_id": "e-1124",
      "problem": "What is the period of the function shown below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14230523/assets/0780a6b1bd6f6d738c9e80e13757ff24d688728aaf8ac306284761b0e1124764.png)",
      "worked_solution": "Note that if we shift the graph $3$ units left or right, the graph remains unchanged.\n\nOn the other hand, if we shift the graph horizontally by any distance other than $3$ (or a multiple other than $3$), we get a different graph.\n\nTherefore, the period of the function is $3.$",
